            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">This postcard shows a color illustration of the Tour Saint-Jacques, a Gothic tower at the southeast angle of the Rue de Rivoli and Boulevard San Sébastopol, representing the remains of the 16th-century Church of Saint-Jacques-la-Boucherie. The image was published in Paris by Éditions d’art “Yvon,” established by Pierre Yves-Petit (1886-1969) (Beatrice Thornton, “Yvon’s Paris,” at http://www.artnet.com/magazineus/reviews/thornton/yvons-paris-1-18-11.asp).</note>
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">“Merry Christmas”. JJ’s idiosyncratic spelling is retained for the texts he writes in Greek. Thanks to Stephanie Nelson for assistance with the Greek.</note> </div>
